-- Passage rg5-authors-purpose-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('851fa0a0-1a99-5d87-9c74-9acbb27a3e53', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Marathon Morning$q$, $q$Account 1: Blog Post by Daniela Okonkwo, First-Time Marathon Runner

On Sunday I ran my first marathon! For four hours I ran right down the middle of streets that are usually full of cars. People cheered from the sidewalks and held up funny signs. Around mile 20, my legs felt as heavy as bricks. Then a girl at a water table handed me a cup and said, "You can do it!" That gave me the push I needed to finish.

Account 2: Letter from Samuel Ortiz, City Bus Driver

On race day, five of the streets on my route were closed. I had to follow a long detour, and many of my riders were late for work. One man missed the start of his shift. I am glad the runners had a good day, and I even honked to cheer them on. But next year, I wish the city would post detour notices at bus stops a week ahead, not the night before.

Account 3: Journal of Mei Lin Chen, Age 11, Volunteer

My mom and I worked at the water table at mile 20. We filled more than 2,000 paper cups. Many runners looked tired, so I shouted encouragement as I held out cups. A lot of them said thank you even while they were out of breath. Afterward, we picked up cups from the street for an hour.$q$, 'draft')
