-- Passage rg5-authors-purpose-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e2fd2a02-b7d1-5075-85f0-ade3e73fe831', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Recess Before Lunch$q$, $q$Account 1: Note to Families from Principal Naomi Adeyemi

This fall, Oakdale Elementary moved recess to before lunch. In the past, many students gulped their food so they could rush outside to play. Now they come to lunch after playing, so they are hungry and in no hurry. In September, our cafeteria threw away 28 bags of food each week, down from 40 last year. We believe this change is good for students' health.

Account 2: From the Class Newspaper, by Ravi Patel, Age 10

At first I loved having recess before lunch. I can eat slowly and talk with my friends. But there is one problem. After recess, everyone has to wash their hands, and the line at the sinks is very long. Sometimes I wait so long that I have only fifteen minutes to eat. I still like the change, but the school needs more sinks or more time.

Account 3: Interview with Bea Kowalski, Cafeteria Worker

The students come in hungry and much calmer than before. I see fewer spilled milk cartons, and more trays come back empty. The change did make one part of my job harder, though. Lunch starts fifteen minutes later now, so I have to keep the hot food warm for longer. Overall, I think the kids are eating better.$q$, 'draft')
